config BLK_DEV_N72_NAND
	bool "Apple S5L8720 FMSS NAND block driver"
	depends on CPU_S5L8720 || COMPILE_TEST
	help
	  Driver for the NAND controller of the iPod touch 2G. Page reads,
	  programs and erases run Apple's sequencer programs, loaded as
	  firmware; without them it can only reset the chips and read their
	  IDs. Apple's VSVFL and YAFTL layers on top present iOS's partitions
	  and an image file on its data partition as disks.

config BLK_DEV_N72_NAND_DEBUG
	bool "Raw test files for the S5L8720 FMSS NAND controller"
	depends on BLK_DEV_N72_NAND
	help
	  Files in sysfs to read the chips' IDs, single pages and the
	  controller's registers, to erase and program blocks of the
	  reserve pool listed in the write_allow parameter, and to check
	  the FTL and write test pages through it beyond what iOS exposes
	  (ftl_check, ftl_test). For work on the driver only.

	  If unsure, say N.
